Our meshing step receives as input a set of vertex-to-vertex matches pi , qj between vertices on the same or different strips. It uses match pairs containing consecutive vertices on each stroke to determine the local meshing strategy (see inset). Given two consecutive match pairs pi , qj and pi+1 , qj+1 (or similarly pi+1 , qj−1) it triangulates the quad pi , pi+1 , qi+1 , qi(or similarly pi , pi+1 , qi − 1,qi  
) using the diagonal that produces a more planar, better shaped triangulation.
Since we expect the mesh to be fair, it discards the quad if the dihedral angle between the resulting triangles is under 45 ◦ .
